    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneIII_20.2/p@71080",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MACBETH.\nThere’s comfort yet; they are assailable.\nThen be thou jocund. Ere the bat hath flown\nHis cloister’d flight, ere to black Hecate’s summons\nThe shard-born beetle, with his drowsy hums,\nHath rung night’s yawning peal, there shall be done\nA deed of dreadful note.",
